      "mods": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "html": "<big><b>SKOL ZERO ZERO</b></big>\nSomewhere along the way, drinking less became a full-time personality. And alcohol-free beers started looking more like supplements than beer.\nTo launch Brazil’s first zero-alcohol, zero-sugar beer, Skol challenged the category’s most unnecessary restriction: having fun.\nInstead of making beer fit into wellness culture, we made wellness fit into beer culture.",
        "align": "left"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "flex": "99 1 0%",
      "mods": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "html": "<small><b>Role</b><br>Creative Direction, Art Direction<br><br><b>With</b><br>Bruno Brux, Rainor Marinho, Gabriel Padilha, Vitor Sotero, Samoel Junqueira</small><br><br><small><b>Production</b><br>Lightfarm Studios</small><br><br><small><b>Agency</b><br>GUT<br><br><b>Client</b><br>Skol<br><br><b>Year</b><br>2026</small>",
        "align": ""
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "embed",
    "src": "https://player.vimeo.com/video/1230714388",
    "ratio": "56.25%"
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "html": "<big>A healthy disrespect for wellness.</big>\n<big>Twenty years later, we brought back one of Skol’s most iconic campaigns. Because if Skol had invented wellness, even healthy habits would be more fun.</big>",
    "align": "center"
   },
   {
    "type": "grid",
